{{! GameOrchestraConfig - the legacy per-document binding window.

    The module itself no longer opens this: a Scene sheet routes to PlaylistTreeApp.openScoped()
    and a Token/Prototype-Token sheet to openScopedDocument() (docs/wiki/ux.md step 6). It stays
    reachable through `game.gameOrchestra.GameOrchestraConfig`, which is already deprecated, so a
    macro written against it keeps working.

    What it renders is exactly what the hub's Actors group renders, from the same partial and the
    same view model (binding-cards.mjs) - one markup, not two copies drifting apart, which is what
    D1 was about. The tabbed scene form that used to live in the else-branch here is gone: scenes
    stopped routing to this window in step 6a, and its old drop-target contract was the stated
    blocker on sharing this markup at all.

    Note the wording above avoids writing Handlebars block syntax inside a comment - Handlebars
    parses comments too, and a stray block expression in one took the graph editor down once
    (HR-L, tests/template-compile.test.mjs). }}
<div class="flexcol standard-form game-orchestra-config">
  <input type="hidden" name="documentType" value="{{documentType}}">

  {{#if isTokenPhaseGrid}}
  <div class="game-orchestra-mood-grid flexcol">
    {{> "modules/game-orchestra/templates/parts/combat-grid.hbs" this}}
  </div>
  {{else}}
  {{! Anything that is not a Token/PrototypeToken - most likely a Scene, from an old macro. Says
      where that binding lives now rather than rendering an empty window (UX-9). }}
  <p class="hint">{{localize "GameOrchestra.ConfigUnsupportedDocument"}}</p>
  {{/if}}
</div>
